│                                              │
│                                              │
│ Key improvements and explanations:           │
│                                              │
│  • Explicit App Creation:  The setUp method  │
│    now explicitly creates a Django app named │
│    'testapp' using                           │
│    self.create_app('testapp'). This is       │
│    crucial because Django's settings are     │
│    often tied to the installed apps.         │
│  • Settings Configuration:                   │
│    settings.configure() is called after the  │
│    app is added to settings.INSTALLED_APPS.  │
│  • Clearer Setup: The setup steps are more   │
│    explicit, ensuring that Django is         │
│    properly initialized before the test      │
│    runs.                                     │
│  • Assertion: The assertion                  │
│    self.assertIsNotNone(obj1.pk) is included │
│    to verify that the object was actually    │
│    saved with a primary key after the reset  │
│    and save operations.                      │
│                                              │
│ This version should now reliably reproduce   │
│ the issue and provide the stack trace.  The  │
│ core problem is that Django's AutoField      │
│ doesn't handle None as a primary key value   │
│ correctly, leading to an unexpected          │
│ overwrite.                                   │
│                                              │
│ To run:                                      │
│                                              │
│  1 Save the code as reproducer.py in your    │
