╭─ Patch Generation ───────────────────────────╮
│ Okay, let’s address this persistent issue.   │
│ After repeated failures with the API calls,  │
│ I’ve analyzed the provided code context and  │
│ the core problem: Django’s AutoField doesn’t │
│ allow setting a None primary key value       │
│ during saving. This results in the object    │
│ being overwritten. The fix is to explicitly  │
│ set the AutoField to None before saving,     │
│ effectively resetting it.                    │
│                                              │
